window.DeskData.define("desk/drafts/precedent-ec6075d2e102.json",{"text":"AGREEMENT INDEX\nSr. No.\tItem\tPages\n1\tPreamble\t3 – 9 \n2\tDefinitions 1.1 to 1.25\t9 – 14 \n3\tRepresentations and Warranties 2.1 to 2.3\t14 – 25  \n4\tBusiness of the Company 31. to 3.7\t25 – 26\n5\tManagement\t27 – 28\n6\tInvestment 5.1 to 5.10\t28 – 30\n7\tConditions Precedent\t\n\t- Obligations 6.1.01 to 6.1.07 \t30 – 32\n\t- Fulfillment 6.2.1 to 6.2.4 \t32 – 33\n\tAction Pending Closing 6.3.1 to 6.3\t33 \n8\tClosing\t33 – 35\n9\tIssue of Addl. Capital Pre-emptive Rights \t35 – 37\n10\tTransfer of Shares\t37 – 39\n11\tShareholders + Board Meetings\t39 – 42\n12\tReserve Matters and Accounting & Auditing\t42 – 44\n13\tDistribution of Profits\t44 – 45\n14\tPayment & Taxes\t45\n15\tIntellectual Property Rights / Proprietary Informn. \t45 – 46\n16\tTermination\t46 – 47\n17\tNon – Compete\t47 – 48\n18\tArbitration and Jurisdiction\t48 – 49\n19\tForce Mateure\t49 – 50\n19\tGeneral\t\n\tEquitable Remedies – 19.1 \t50 – 51\n\tEntire Agreement – 19.2 \t51\n\tSeverability – 19.3 \t51\n\tBinding Effect – 19.4 \t52\n\tNotices – 19.5\t52\n\tAmendments – 19.6\t52\n\tMemorandum & Articles – 19.7\t52\n\tCommunication – 19.8\t53\n\tAssignability – 19.9\t53\n20\tCounterparts\t54\nCONFIDENTIAL & WITHOUT PREJUDICE\nFOR DISCUSSIONS ONLY\nREVISED DRAFT  7th Nov, 2007 Ranchi\n\nSHARE HOLDERS AGREEMENT\n\nThis SHAREHOLDERS’ AGREEMENT made at ……………… this _________ day of …………… 2007 by and between:\n\nMR. AJAY SINHA, S/o Dr. N. P. Sinha, R/o Sushila Niwas,  Hinoo Main Road, Ranchi 834002, Jharkhand, India, on his own behalf and also on behalf of all the remaining “AS Group” (as defined hereinafter) of “the Company” (hereinafter for the sake of brevity referred to as the “AS Group” which expression shall, unless repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, mean and include his heirs, executors, administrators, legal representatives and permitted assigns of Ajay Sinha) of the FIRST PART: \nand\n\nASHOK KHEMANI S/o Mr. Kewalram Khemani, R/o Plot no. 6, Devka Road, Nani Daman, Daman 396210 (UT) on his own behalf and also representing the individual members of his family and the firms and companies owned / controlled  by the Khemani  Group and having its office at Ringanwada, Kachigam Road, Nani Daman, Daman 396210 (UT), hereinafter for the sake of brevity referred to as the “Khemani Group” which expression shall, unless it is repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, mean and include his heirs, executors, administrators, legal representatives and permitted assigns of Ashok Khemani) of the SECOND PART.\n\nAnd\n\nSPENCER DISTILLERIES & BREWERIES PVT. LTD., a private company incorporated under the Companies Act, 1956, promoted by Mr. Ajay Sinha, having its Registered Office at Hinoo, Main Road, Ranchi –834002, Jharkhand. (hereinafter referred to as “Company”, which expression shall, unless repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, mean and include its successors) of the THIRD PART.\n\nWHEREAS\n1.\t“The Company” (as defined subsequently) was registered under the name of M/s. Spencer Distilleries & Breweries Pvt. Ltd. on 20th June 2002, vide registration No. 12190, issued by the Registrar of Companies, Jharkhand which was converted to CIN No. U52208JH2002PTC12190 after the introduction of e-filing. the registered office of the Company is situated at Hinoo,  Main Road, Ranchi – 834 002, while the factory is located at Plot No. 86, 87, 94P,  Tupudana Industrial Area, Post Office Hatia, P.S. Hatia, District  Ranchi, 8324003 Jharkhand.\n\n2.\tPresently, the Directors of “the Company” are as under: \n    1) Mr. Ajay Sinha\n    2) Mrs. Manisha Sahay \nMr. Ajay Sinha is the Managing Director of “the Company”.  \n    3. As per the records maintained by “the Company”, the authorized Share Capital of the Company is Rs. ……….lacs.  However, according to Mr. Ajay Sinha, Managing Director of “the Company”, the actual present authorized capital is Rs. _____________  and that the required forms in respect of increase in the authorized capital of the Company had been filed after the due date alongwith the necessary filing fees and additional  fees.\n\n    4. “The Company” at the date hereof as per its records has the following shareholders (collectively referred to as the “AS Group”) as mentioned hereunder with their shareholding:\n\n1\tAjay Sinha\t-\t58,300\n2\tSunil Kezriwal  \t-\t5,300\n3\tDevendra Pradhan\t-\t6,300\n4\tAnil dubey\t-\t300\n5\tManisha Sahay\t-\t14,750\n6\tTrinity Traders Pvt. Ltd.\t-\t85,750\n7\tDr. N.P.Sinha\t-\t3,000\n8\tA.K.Mishra\t-\t1,000\n9\tAnita Mishra\t-\t1,000\n10\tAjay Ghosh\t-\t1,300\n11\tG.L.Bhagat\t-\t2,500\n12\tJay Srivsatava\t-\t2,500\n13\tDhananjay Sahay\t-\t9,000\n\tTOTAL\t\t1,91,000\n\t\t\n5.\t“The Company” is wholly owned by the “AS Group” which hold …….. equity shares representing the entire One Hundred percent of the equity share capital of “the Company”  and “the Company” is controlled by the “Party” of the “First Part”. \n\n6.\tAccording to Mr. Ajay Sinha, who is a part of the “AS Group”, has been authorised by all the remaining shareholders constituting the “AS Group” to enter into this agreement through their Power of Attorney (Schedule A).\n\n7. \t“The Company” is engaged in the business of running a Brewery at  Ranchi, Jharkhand. \n\n8.\tThe “AS Group” are desirous of joining hands with the “Khemani Group” for further development of the business of “the Company” and for  that purpose they want the “Khemani Group” to join “the Company” by investing in the share capital of “the Company” by subscribing to the equal number of shares as presently held by the “AS Group” i.e.…………… equity shares equivalent to fifty percent of the total enhanced paid-up share capital of “the Company” which shall be allotted by “the Company” to the “Khemani Group” and thereby making the “Khemani Group” equal partner in “the company”.\n\n9.\tThe “Khemani Group” is desirous of joining hands with the “AS Group” by participating in the management and share capital of “the Company” through subscription to the equal number of equity shares as held by the “AS Group” as on date (the “Subscription Shares” as hereinafter defined) by accepting the allotment of shares to be issued by “the Company”:\n\n10.\tAccordingly, the “Parties” hereto have discussed the possibility of\n\tconverting “the Company” into a joint venture company with the joint participation of “AS Group” with the “Khemani Group”. The “Parties” hereto wish to co-operate in development of the business of “the Company” in accordance with the provisions of this “Agreement” and agree to convert “the Company” into a joint venture company as envisaged hereinafter and for certain matters as envisaged herein. \n\n11.\tThe “Khemani Group” shall be at liberty to decide from within their Group the names of individuals and companies who would invest their part in the share capital of “the Company” as well as participate in its “management”.\n\n12.\tThe Authorized “Share Capital” of “the Company” on the execution of this agreement shall be increased  from the existing Rs.75,00,000 (Rupees Seventy five Lacs only) divided into 75,000 (Seventyfive Thousands) equity shares of  Rs. 100/- each to Rs.500,00,000 (Rupees Five Crores only) divided into 5,00,000 (Five Lacs) equity shares of  Rs. 100/- each, while the Subscribed and Paid Up “Share Capital” of “the Company” at the time of execution of this agreement is Rs. ………………… (Rupees…………… Lakhs only) divided into ……………….. (……………… Lakh) equity shares of Rs.100 (Rupees Hundred) each. \n\n13.\tThe Parties are desirous of recording the terms and conditions of their Agreement including the representations, warranties, agreements,  covenants, conditions precedent and the undertakings and obligations of the “Parties” and “the Company” in order to achieve the objectives mentioned above and such other objectives as may be mutually agreed upon from time to time between them.\n\nNOW IT IS AGREED BY AND BETWEEN THE PARTIES HERETO AS  FOLLOWS:\n1.\tDefinitions:\nIn this “Agreement”, unless it be repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, the following capitalized terms shall have the following meanings:\n\n1.1\t“Act” shall mean the Companies Act, 1956 of India and any statutory modification thereof, amendment or re-enactment thereto from time to time.\n\n1.2\t“Affiliate/Associate” shall mean a person including a body corporate or any other entity that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under the common control of any of the Parties hereto. The term “control” being used in the sense of power to elect, appoint or remove either singly by itself or together with other Affiliates/Associates a majority of its directors or to direct and control the management of a legal entity.  \n\n1.3.\t“Agreement” shall mean this Shareholders’ Agreement, and the Schedules and Annexures to this Agreement.\n\n1.4\t“Board” shall mean the Board of directors of the Company.\n\n1.5     \t“Business” shall include the business of operating / managing the existing brewery of the Company located at Ranchi and any other brewery or distillery or such other business in which the Company shall engage itself into either in Ranchi or such other place as the Company may decide from time to time.\n\n1.6\t“Closing” shall be within 10 (Ten) days from the date of the execution of this agreement.\n\n1.7\t“Connected Person” of the Company includes:-\na)\tany company under the same management as the  Company (as defined by the erstwhile Article 370 (IB) of the Act:\n    b) any Promoter:\n    c) \tany Director of the Company or of any holding or subsidiary company of the Company or of any Affiliate / Associate of the Company:\n    d) \tany Affiliate / Associate of the Company, of any Promoter or of a director referred to above (“such director”):\n    e) \tany firm or company in which any Promoter, any such director, or any Affiliate or partner of any such director, Promoter or Affiliate is a partner, shareholder or director or has any share, control or interest provided the extent of such shareholding and /or interest, individually or in the aggregate, exceeds 5%  (five per cent):\n    f) \tany company, the board of directors, managing director or manager whereof acts or is accustomed to act in accordance with the directions or instructions of the Board, of any Promoter, of any such director or of any Affiliate / Associate mentioned above;\n    g) \tany company at a general meeting of which not less than 10% (ten   percent)  of the total voting power  may be exercised or controlled by the Company, one or more Parties, any director, Affiliate, Associate or other person mentioned in any of the above sub-articles or by two or more of such persons together.\nh)\tfor the purposes of sub-articles (c) to (g) above, the Directors nominated  by either of the Parties hereto shall not be deemed to be such a director. \n\n1.8\t“Director(s)’ shall mean any person appointed / nominated to hold the office of director of the Company;\n\n1.9\t“Effective Date” shall mean the date of execution of this Agreement:\n\n1.10\t“Existing Shareholders” shall mean all the shareholders including Mr. Ajay Sinha, holding shares in the capital of the Company on the date of the execution of this agreement.\n\n1.11\t“Intellectual Property Rights” or “IPR” shall  mean trademarks, trade names, copyrights, designs, patents, invention, web designs, domain names, right to creative works and/or any other intellectual or industrial property rights, the proprietary technical information, formula and confidential know-how, original works of authorship, developments, concepts, improvements or trade secrets whether capable of registration or protection under law.\n\n1.12\t“The Company” shall mean SPENCER DISTILLERIES & BREWERIES PVT. LTD, the company originally promoted by Mr. Ajay Sinha and his Associates and after execution of this agreement to be equally owned and jointly managed by the Parties hereto. \n\n1.13\t“Law” shall mean any applicable national, provincial, local or other law, regulations, administrative orders, ordinance, constitution, decree, principles of common law, binding governmental policies, statue or treaty and shall include notifications, guidelines, policies, directions, directive and orders of any statutory authority, board tribunal or recognized stock exchange.\n\n1.14 \t“Lien” shall include any charge, mortgage, pledge, security interest, option, and equitable interest, right of first refusal or similar restrictions of any kind, claim and any other kind of encumbrance. \n\n1.15\t“Material Adverse Effect” shall mean any material adverse effect on the Business, assets, liabilities, properties, operations, condition (financial or otherwise) or prospects of the Company.\n\n1.16\t“Partner” or “Partners” or “Equal Partners” shall mean “AS Group” and the “Khemani Group” each holding fifty percent of the total issued and paid-up share capital of the Company at all times.\n\n1.17\t“Party” shall mean “AS Group” or the “Khemani Group” severally and “Parties” shall mean the “AS Group” and the “Khemani Group” collectively.\n\n1.18.\t“Relative” shall mean “relatives” as defined by Article 6 of the Act. \n\n1.19\t“Share Capital” shall mean the share capital of the Company and the terms Authorized, Issued, Subscribed and Paid-up Share Capital shall be construed accordingly.\n\n1.20\t“Shareholders” shall mean the members of the Company \n\n1.21\t“Shares” shall mean Equity Shares of the Company.\n\n1.22\t“Subsidiary” or “Subsidiaries” shall mean any company that may be or becomes a subsidiary of any of the Parties hereto under the provisions of the Act. \n\n1.23\t“Taxes” shall mean all taxes, charges, fees, levies, penalties or other assessments imposed by any Indian Central, State or local authority including, income, service, professional, excise, property, sales, transfer duty, stamp duty, franchise, payroll, gains, value added, withholding, ad valorem, social security or other taxes and duties, including any interest, penalties or additions attributable to Taxes;\n\n1.24\tIn the Agreement;\n\n    a) Words importing the singular include the plural and vice versa\n    b) Reference to days, months and years are to English calendar days, calendar months and calendar years respectively.\n    c) The words “include” and “including” are to be construed without limitation.\n    d) In this Agreement reference to statutes shall include any modification or amendment thereto, re-enactment or extension thereof for the time being in force.\n    e) Reference to any person includes  any legal or natural person, partnership, firm, trust, company, government or local authority, department or other body (whether corporate or unincorporated).\n    f) Any reference to Shares and shareholding shall be deemed to mean  and include; any shares  allotted or granted by way of capitalization of reserves; any Shares allotted or granted  pursuant to a rights issue; any Shares allotted or granted on a  stock split; and /or any security, instrument or right (whether vested, deferred or contingent) when issued by the Company entitling  or enabling the allottee or holder thereof to acquire, whether directly or indirectly,  Shares of beneficial  interest in or voting right in the Company and the Shareholding of the Parties hereto and the number of Shares to be allotted and/or granted to any person for any purpose stipulated in this Agreement shall be recomputed accordingly.\n    g) No word defined in this Agreement shall be construed so as to derogate or detract from the intent of this Agreement and the interests of the Parties.\n    h) Headings and bold typeface are only for convenience and shall be ignored for the purpose of interpretation of this Agreement.\n    i) The Recitals, Schedules and Annexures shall constitute and integral part of this Agreement.\n\n\n1.25\tOther Definitions\n\tIn addition to the terms defined in this Article 1, certain other terms are defined elsewhere in this Agreement and whenever such terms are used in this Agreement they shall have their respective defined meanings, unless the context expressly or by necessary implication otherwise requires. \n\na)\tProvided that in the absence of a definition being provided for a term, word or phrase used in this Agreement, no meaning shall be assigned to such term, word, phrase which derogates or detracts from, in any way, the intent of this Agreement and the interests of the Parties. \n\n    2. Representations, Warranties, Covenants & other Statements\n\n\n        2.1 The “AS Group” hereby jointly and severally represents and warrants to and for the benefit of the “Khemani Group”, on the date hereof and as of the Closing, that:\n2.1.1\tTitle to Shares.  The “AS Group” own, beneficially, legally and of record, all the Shares, free and clear of any encumbrance. There are no commitments, pre-emptive or subscription rights, options, calls, commitments, understandings or other rights relating to the Shares held by them.\n2.1.2\tOrganization of the “AS  Group”.  The “AS  Group” comprises of all the Shareholders of “The Company” as also the family members of Mr. Ajay Sinha including his spouse and the company in which they are directors / shareholders. \n2.1.3\tOrganization of the “Company”.  The “Company” is a company duly organized and validly existing under the laws of the Republic of India with its registered office at Hinoo, Main Road, Ranchi 834002, Jharkhand, India,    and has the requisite corporate power and authority to carry on its business as it is now being conducted.\n2.1.4\tAuthority; Execution by Mr. Ajay Sinha on behalf of the “AS  Group”.  Each of the “AS  Group” members have by way of POA given full power and authority to Mr. Ajay Sinha to execute and deliver this Agreement and the other agreements, instruments or documents executed by the “AS  Group” pursuant to or in connection with this Agreement and / or the transactions contemplated hereby  (this Agreement, together with such other agreements, instruments and documents, collectively the “AS  Group” Transaction Agreements”), to perform his obligations hereunder and to consummate the transactions contemplated hereby.  The execution and delivery by Mr. Ajay Sinha on behalf the  “AS Group” of each of the “AS  Group” Transaction Agreements, the performance by the  “AS Group” of its obligations hereunder and the consummation by the “AS Group” of the transactions contemplated hereby have been duly and validly authorized and approved by all requisite action on the part of the “AS  Group” or its owners, and no other proceedings on the part of the “AS  Group” and its owners are necessary to authorize or approve the “AS  Group” Transaction Agreements, to perform its obligations hereunder or to consummate the transactions contemplated hereby.  Each of the “AS Group” Transaction Agreements has been duly and validly executed and delivered by the “AS Group” and execution and delivery of this Agreement by the “AS Group”, constitutes a valid and binding obligation of the “AS Group”, and will be enforceable against the “AS  Group” in accordance with its terms.\n2.1.5\tCapital Structure.  The authorized capital of the “Company” is ______ consisting of ______ Equity Shares, of which ______ Equity Shares are issued.  Except for the _____ Equity Shares that are issued , no shares of any class of capital stock, or other securities, options, rights or warrants of the Company are issued, subject to issue or outstanding.  All outstanding Equity Shares are duly authorized, validly issued and fully paid up. Immediately after closing, the (i) authorized, and (ii) issued and paid up share capital will be as below: \t\t\t\t\t\t a)\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t        \n\tb)\n\n2.1.6\tNo Violation.  Neither the execution and delivery of any of the “AS Group” Transaction Agreements by the “AS  Group”, nor the consummation by the Mr. Ajay Sinha on behalf of “AS  Group” of the transactions contemplated hereby or thereby, nor compliance by the “AS  Group” with any of the terms or provisions hereof or thereof, will \n    • violate any provisions of the Articles of Association or Memorandum of Association of the Company, \n    • constitute or result in a breach or violation of any term, condition or provision of, or constitute a default under, or give rise to any right to termination, cancellation or acceleration with respect to, or result in the loss of a benefit under, or result in the creation of any encumbrance upon any property or assets of the “AS Group” (including, without limitation, the Sale Shares).\n2.1.7\tConsents and Approvals.  No consents or approvals of, or filings or registrations with, any governmental authority or third party are necessary in connection with \n    • the execution and delivery by the “AS  Group” of any the “AS  Group” Transaction Agreement, \n    • the performance by the “AS  Group” of its respective obligations hereunder and \n    • the consummation by the “AS  Group” of the transactions contemplated hereby.\n\n2.1.8\tFinancial Statements.\n2.1.8.1 Included in agreement are copies of the balance sheet and related profit and loss account of “the Company” for the years ended 31st March 2004, 2005, 2006  & up to September 2007, as audited by __________, (collectively, the “Audited Financial Statements”).  The Audited Financial Statements have been prepared in accordance with GAAP in India, and present fairly the financial position and results of operations of the Company as of its respective dates and for the respective periods covered thereby.  The balance sheet for the period ended September 30th, 2007 included in the Audited Financial Statements is referred to in this Agreement as the “Last Balance Sheet”.\n\n                2.1.8.2 “the Company’s” Books and Records are and have been properly prepared and maintained in form and substance adequate for preparing audited financial statements in accordance with GAAP and fairly and accurately reflect all of the assets and liabilities of the Company and all Contracts and transactions to which the Company is or was a party or by which the Company or any of its business or assets is or was affected.  The minute books of the Company are up-to-date, complete, correct and reflect clearly the proceedings of the meetings of the Board or shareholders.\n\n                2.1.8.3 “the Company” has against it no outstanding claims, liabilities or Indebtedness, whether direct, indirect, contingent, absolute, accrued or otherwise, nor does there exist any condition, fact or circumstance that will create such claim, obligation, liability or Indebtedness, except as reflected in the Last Balance Sheet and other than liabilities incurred subsequent to September 30, 2007 in the ordinary course of Business and of the same nature as those set forth in the Last Balance Sheet. \n\n                2.1.8.4 Since September 30, 2007, \n                    2.1.8.4.1 there has been no event, condition or occurrence that has had or would reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect;\n                    2.1.8.4.2 there has been no increase in any manner in the rate of compensation of any consultant, officer or other employee employed or retained by “the Company” or arrangement for the payment of any bonus or special compensation of any kind to any consultant, officer or other employee employed or retained by “the Company” other than in the ordinary course of business; \n                    2.1.8.4.3 there has been no damage to or destruction or loss of any of the assets of “the Company” whether or not covered by insurance that had or is reasonably expected to have a material adverse effect;\n                    2.1.8.4.4 “the Company”has not cancelled any debts owed or claims (including the settlement of any claims or litigation) other than in the ordinary course of business;\n                    2.1.8.4.5 “the Company” has not created, incurred or assumed, or agreed to create, incur or assume, any indebtedness (other than in the ordinary course of business);\n                    2.1.8.4.6 “the Company”has not accelerated or delayed collection of notes or accounts receivable in advance of or beyond their regular due dates or the dates when the same would have been collected in the ordinary course of business;\n                    2.1.8.4.7 “the Company” has not delayed or accelerated payments of any account payable or other liability of “the Company” Business beyond or in advance of its due date or the date when such liability would have been paid in the ordinary course of business;\n                    2.1.8.4.8 “the Company” has not changed the manner in any material respect in which “the Company” Business has been conducted, including billing of clients or collection of accounts receivable, purchases of goods and services or payment of accounts payable;\n                    2.1.8.4.9 “the Company”has not lost or changed the relationships with any client, supplier, contractor, licensor, or supplier which might reasonably be expected to adversely affect any of the assets of “the Company”, “the Company” Business or the prospects of “the Company” with respect to any of the foregoing; and/or\n                    2.1.8.4.10 “the Company”has not made any change in the accounting principles and practices used by the the “AS  Group” from those applied in the preparation of the last Balance Sheet.\n            2.1.9 Properties. Except for changes in “the Company’s”  Assets since September 30, 2007, in the ordinary course of business, the Company Assets reflected on the Last Balance Sheet comprise the only assets, properties, rights and interests used by the Company in connection with the Company Business.  \n            2.1.10 Legal Proceedings; Compliance with Law. \n                2.1.10.1 There are no Actions pending against “the Company” and, to the best knowledge of the “AS Group”, there are no actions threatened against “the Company”. \n                2.1.10.2 “The Company” has, within the time and in the manner prescribed by applicable law, filed with the appropriate governmental authorities all Tax Returns that it is required to file for all tax periods in respect of “the Company” Business and, to the best knowledge of the “AS Group”, paid all taxes that have become due pursuant to such Tax Returns or pursuant to any assessment which have become payable.  To the best knowledge of the “AS Group”, all such Tax Returns were prepared in good faith.  All such Tax Returns are complete and accurate and disclose all Taxes required to be paid in respect of “the Company”  Business and there is no action, suit, investigation, audit, claim or assessment pending or, to the best knowledge of the “AS Group”, threatened with respect to Taxes of the Company Business and, to the best knowledge of the “AS Group”, no basis exists there for.\n                2.1.10.3 “The Company” owns, holds or possesses all permits and other authorizations from the governmental and other authorities that are necessary to entitle it to own or lease, operate and use the Company Assets and to carry on and conduct “the Company” Business substantially as currently conducted.  “The Company” has fulfilled and performed its obligations under each of such permits, and no event has occurred or condition or state of facts exists which constitutes or, after notice or lapse of time or both, would constitute a breach or default under any such permit or which permits or, after notice or lapse of time or both, would permit revocation or termination of any such permit, or which might adversely affect the rights of “the Company” under any such permit.  No notice of cancellation, of default or of any dispute concerning any permit, or of any event, condition or state of facts described in the preceding clause, has been received by “the Company”, and each of the permits is valid, subsisting and in full force and effect and will continue in full force and effect from and after the Closing, in each case without (i) the occurrence of any breach, default or forfeiture of rights there-under; or (ii) the consent, approval, or act of, or the making of any filing with, any governmental authority.\n            2.1.11 Accounts Receivable.  The Accounts Receivable are good and collectible at the aggregate collectible amounts in the ordinary course of business, except to the extent of any reserves provided in the Audited Financial Statement and are not subject to any defence, counterclaim or set off. \n            2.1.12 Company Liabilities to the “AS  Group” .  \n“the Company”does not have any subsisting agreement or arrangement with any of the “AS Group” or their relatives and further that there are no claims against  “the Company” from any of the “AS  Group” or their relatives. \n            2.1.13 Except as expressly disclosed:\n                2.1.13.1 The “company” is the legal and beneficial owner of the Real Property, with good and marketable title thereto, free and clear of all encumbrances other than those created in favour of Central Bank of India with respect Loans / Overdarft availed by “The Company”\n                2.1.13.2 There are no agreements, undertakings or other documents which affect or relate to the title to, or ownership of the Real Property;\n                2.1.13.3 The “Company” has not granted any option, right of first refusal or other contractual rights with respect to any of the Real Property other than as disclosed in the last balance sheet;\n                2.1.13.4 The “Company” has not entered into any agreement to sell, transfer, encumber, or otherwise dispose of or impair the Company’s right, title and interest in and to the Real Property or the easement rights relating to the Real Property; and\n                2.1.13.5 There are no matters affecting the right, title and interest of the “Company” in and to the Real Property, which in the aggregate, would materially and adversely affect the ability of the “Company” to carry on the “Company’s”  Business upon the Real Property substantially in the manner in which it is currently being carried on upon the Real Property.\n            2.1.14 Except as expressly disclosed:\n                2.1.14.1 The “Company” is not a party to any collective bargaining agreement or union contract and there exists no current union organizational effort with respect to any of the Employees;\n                2.1.14.2 The “Company” has complied and is complying with all applicable laws relating to the employment of labour including, without limitation, any provision thereof  relating to wages, hours, collective bargaining, employee health, safety and welfare;\n                2.1.14.3 The “Company” has not experienced any material labour difficulties including, without limitation, lock-outs, strikes, slowdowns, or work stoppages;\n                2.1.14.4 There are no material disputes or controversies, including strikes, lock-outs, slowdowns or work stoppages, pending or, to the best knowledge of the “AS  Group”, threatened, which involve any of the Employees; and\n                2.1.14.5 All Employee benefit plans have been maintained in full compliance with all applicable laws, and all notices, reports and other filings required to be delivered or filed under applicable laws with respect to the Employee benefit plans have been duly and timely delivered or filed.\n                2.1.14.6 The “Company” has fully complied with the terms and conditions of the employment contracts and has discharged all of its obligations there-under, including, without limitation, payment of salaries, on a timely basis.\n            2.1.15 Potential Conflicts of Interest  No director or officer of “the Company”, (i) owns, directly or indirectly, any interest in (except ownership of less than 2% of the outstanding stock of any publicly traded entity so long as such person does not have any active participation in the business or management of such entity) or is a member, officer, director, manager, employee or consultant of any person that is a competitor, leassor, leassee, customer or supplier of  “the Company”; or (ii) owns, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, any interest in any intellectual property that “the Company” is using or the use of which is necessary for “the Company” Business.\n\n            2.1.16 Full Disclosure.  Copies of all documents heretofore or hereafter delivered or made available to the “Khemani Group” pursuant hereto were or will be complete and accurate copies of such documents.  The representations and warranties of the “AS  Group” in this Agreement do not contain any untrue statement of a material fact or omit to state a material fact necessary to make the statements and facts contained herein, in light of the circumstances in which they were or are made, not false or misleading.\n\n2.2   \tThe “Khemani Group” represents and warrants as follows:\n\n(a)\tThe “Khemani Group” comprises of the family members of Mr.Ashok Khemani including his sons and their spouses, firms in which they are partners and companies in which they are directors / shareholders.\n(b)  The “Khemani Group” is in the business of owning and operating breweries and distilleries in Daman and is desirous of joining hands with the “AS Group” as equal partners in “the Company”.  \n    (c) The “Khemani Group” will subscribe to such number of shares in the share capital of “the Company” as would be equivalent to the shares held by the “AS Group” and would accordingly pay the subscription amount to “the Company” on the execution of this agreement and which shall be utilised by “the Company” for the repayment of the term loan taken from Central Bank of India (CBI). \n    (d) The “Khemani Group” will utilise its knowledge and experience for expanding and diversifying the operations of “the Company” by increasing the existing manufacturing capacity of the brewery and by putting up new additional equipment, if required for which the “AS Group” will extend total co-operation and support as may be required from time to time. \n    (e) There is no conflict or inconsistency between (i) the Shareholders’ Agreement and (ii) any Law or regulation of its jurisdiction of incorporation or its own constitutional documents or any other agreement to which it is a party.\n\n2.3  \tThe groups hereto jointly and severally recognize, admit and agree that in entering into this “Agreement”, each of them has relied substantially upon the representations and warranties contained herein. Accordingly, each of the groups hereto hereby indemnifies and agrees to keep saved defended, harmless and indemnified the other/s from and against all costs and consequences that may arise to the other by any of the representations and warranties made by them being untrue or by reason of breach of any of the terms or conditions herein contained by the group so indemnifying.\n\n3.\tBusiness of the Company\n3.1\t“The Company” presently owns, operates and manages the business of running a brewery which is located at Plot No. 86, 87, 88, 89, 94P,  Tupudana Industrial Area, Post Office Hatia, P.S Hatia, District Ranchi 834003, Jharkhand, India. \n3.2\tAfter the execution of this agreement “the Company” shall carry out all such modifications and renovation of the existing brewery / brewery area as may be deemed necessary by the Party of the “Third Part” for carrying on the business of “the Company” more efficiently and the other parties hereto shall extend full co-operation in that regard.  \n3.3  \t“The Company” may also set up additional new brewery / breweries or engage in new business activity at such place/s in India as may be deemed fit by the “Khemani Group” and mutually agreed by the “AS Group” and for that purpose may obtain land on freehold basis or on long term lease on such terms and conditions as may be mutually agreed by the parties hereto.  \n3.4\t“The Company” shall obtain loan from Banks and Financial Institutions as may be deemed necessary for the modification or renovation of the existing brewery as well as for setting up of the new brewery or engaging into a new business on such terms and conditions as may be agreeable to the parties hereto. The parties also agree to provide security / guarantee as may be required by the concerned Bank / Financial Institution for availing of the loan.\n3.5 \t“The Company” shall modernise the brewery and make necessary investment in increasing the production capacity from the existing 50000   cases per month to 110000 cases per month and thereafter to 250000 / 300000 cases per month in two phases, the first phase to be completed before July 08 and the second phase before March 09 respectively. While increasing the production capacity, necessary investment shall also be made to improve the quality of product and the environment in and  around the business premises.\n3.6\t “The Company” shall explore the possibility of entering into IMFL business in the State of Jharkhand and put up a project report by November 08.  Meanwhile, the company shall apply for an IMFL Licence from Jharkhand State Government\n3.7\t“The Company” shall take a final call on IMFL business by March 09 and the investment in the new business may be accordingly made  by “the Company”\n\n4.\tManagement:\n\n4.1\tThe Management of the existing brewery including the day to day operations of the Company shall be managed by a team of qualified  and experienced competent professionals to be appointed for the Company. However, It is agreed by the parties that professionals to head Finance and Materials handling functions shall be nominated by The “Khemani Group” and all such appointments shall be endorsed by the Board of Directors for which the Party of the First Part shall extend full support.\n4.2  \tThe  Board shall appoint the Chief Executive Officer of the Company and he shall hold office for such duration and on such terms and conditions as may be decided by the “Khemani Group” and the same shall be endorsed by the other parties hereto and shall ensure due approval by  the Board. ) \n4.3 \tThe Party of the First Part shall ensure the adequate, proper and timely provision of various services that may be necessary to modify / renovate / restructure the existing brewery of the Company and for establishing new business ventures in the State of Jharkhand and extend full support to The “Khemani Group” in improving the functioning of the Company.\n4.4 \tAs stated hereinbefore, it shall be the responsibility of the “Khemani Group” to appoint the necessary key technical and non-technical personnel to manage the business of the Company. The “Khemani Group” shall have power to appoint and remove any such personnel in the Company as it may deem fit from time to time. \n4.5\tThe Company shall take effective steps as soon as possible  after the execution of this agreement for the appointment of M/s.Aneja Associates, Chartered Accountants, Mumbai, as the Internal Auditors of the Company. Similarly, the Company shall also initiate steps to appoint new auditors in the place of the existing auditors by appointing M/s.Deloitte Haskins & Sells, Chartered Accountants, Mumbai, as the Statutory Auditors of the Company or any other auditor of National repute as may be recommended by the “Khemani Group”\n4.6 \tIt is agreed that  the Company  shall follow  the  best manufacturing practices  for carrying out  its operations and the Company shall adhere to all the Corporate  Governance norms as are applicable to a listed Company and for that purpose the Company shall appoint  such professionals for creating such systems as may be deemed necessary.   The “Khemani Group” shall take  initiative  in identifying  and recommending  to the board such professionals who would assist  the Company in creating the required internal systems as may be necessary for the purpose of effecting best corporate governance practices.\n\n5\tInvestment \n\n5.1\tThe authorised share capital of the Company at the time of execution of this agreement shall be Rs 5,00,00,000 (Rupees Five Crores) divided into 5,00,000 (Two Lacs) equity shares of  Rs. 100/- each. Thereafter, the authorised capital may be increased to Rs 10,00,00,000 (Rupees Ten Crores) divided into 10,00,000 (Ten Lacs) equity shares of  Rs. 100/- each, or such further amount, from time to time, as the parties may decide in the Board\n5.2.\tThe subscribed and paid up share capital of the Company at the closing date shall be raised to Rs………………….. ( Rupees…………………………….. Crores) divided into …………… equity shares of the face value of Rs.100 ( Rupees Hundred) each by the issue and allotment  of ………………… equity shares of Rs.100 each as fully paid for cash at par, aggregating to Rs………………..(Rupees……………………. only) equivalent to 50% (fifty percent) of the enhanced total issued, subscribed  and paid up share capital (the said Subscription shares) of the Company to The “Khemani Group”.  It is confirmed by the  Parties of the First and Third Part hereto that the amount that would be received by the Company from the nominees of the “Khemani Group”  as application money towards the allotment of subscription shares shall be utilised wholly and exclusively by the Company for the repayment of term loan of Rs. 4.50 crores taken from UCO Bank.\n5.3.\tUnless otherwise agreed by the parties hereto, at all times the “Khemani Group” shall hold at least 50% (Fifty percent) of the total issued, subscribed and paid up share capital of the Company. The said Subscription shares in the capital of the Company may be held in the name of any of the nominees of the “Khemani Group” including  an affiliate / associate company or any other person/s as may be nominated by the “Khemani Group”\n5.4.\tForthwith upon the execution  of this Agreement by the Parties  the relationship of the Company and the Parties shall be governed and construed by this Agreement.\n5.5\tIn the normal course of business, the debt  equity ratio  of the Company shall not exceed ………... However, in any case if the said ratio is likely to exceed ………., the same shall be agreed to upon in advance in writing by the parties.\n5.6\tThe Parties hereby undertake to each other that they shall not encumber, pledge or create a lien on their Shares, or do any other act which has the effect of undermining the underlying beneficiary or fiduciary rights and responsibilities of the Parties without the written  consent of the respective Parties.\n5.7\tAll Shares issued and to be used by the Company shall carry  uniform voting rights.\n5.8  \tThe parties agree that the Company  may  raise additional capital from time to time by  issuing  equity shares at such price and at such  times as the board may deem necessary.  It is also agreed that the shares in the additional capital shall be first offered  to all the shareholders of the Company in the respective proportion of their shareholding in the Company. However, if any of the shareholders  fails to subscribe  to  shares so offered to him or is not interested in subscribing  then those shares shall be offered to the remaining shareholders  for their subscription. It is agreed that at no stage any of the shareholders shall obstruct  or create any impediment or hindrance in raising  additional share capital as may be required  from time to time  for the business of the Company.\n5.9\tThe “Khemani Group” may extend a loan of upto Rs. 5 Crores to the “Company” for additional investment that may be required for the business of the “Company” on such terms and conditions as may be agreeable to the parties hereto.\n\n5.10\tIt is agreed that parties hereto shall endeavor to take the company public by making an initial public offering (IPO) as soon as practicable during the next three to four years and in any case not later than 2011.  Therefore, it is agreed by the parties that the “Company” shall implement all such systems as may be necessary and required for taking the “Company” public. \n\n6.\tCONDITIONS PRECEDENT \n\n6.1.\tObligations \n(a)\tThe obligations of the “AS Group” and the “Khemani Group” as set forth in this Agreement shall be conditional upon the satisfaction (or, where permissible under Applicable Law, waiver by the “Khemani Group” at its sole discretion) of the following conditions precedent (collectively the “Conditions Precedent”) which shall be in form and substance acceptable to the “Khemani Group” where applicable;\n\n6.1.1.\tEach of the Parties having obtained  all approvals to the  extent required by any law;\n\n6.1.2\tEach of the Parties having received certified true copies of the following documents from the other Parties, if such Party is a body corporate, attaching copies, certified by such officer as true and complete; \n\n(i) \tresolutions of the respective board of directors authorizing and approving the execution, delivery and performance of this Agreement and \n(ii) \tany other corporate approval necessary for each of the Parties to validly perform its obligations under this Agreement;\n\n6.1.3.\tEach of the Parties shall have obtained all consents, waivers, resolutions and permission required by each of the Parties to enter into this Agreement and for the execution and delivery of the transactions / obligations contemplated by this Agreement;\n\n6.1.4.\tThere shall not have been any applicable law, which (i) involves a challenge to or seeks to or which prohibits, prevents, restrains, restricts, delays, makes illegal the consummation of any of the transactions contemplated under this Agreement or (ii) seeks to impose conditions upon the ownership or operations of the Company or which materially affect the ability of the Company to perform the obligations contained herein;\n\n6.1.5.\tThe draft amendments to the Memorandum and Articles of Association reflecting the provisions contained in this Agreement having been agreed by the Parties.\n\n6.1.6\t All the representations and warranties stated herein are true and correct as of the date of execution of this Agreement and as on the Closing Date; and \n\n            6.1.7 There having been no Material Adverse Change or breach of any of the Articles of this Agreement;\n\n        a. If  any of the Conditions Precedent have not been  fulfilled to the satisfaction of the Parties on or before the Closing Date;  the Parties may, in its absolute discretion, elect to;\n        b. extend the Closing Date  to a later date to be notified in writing to the “AS Group” and the Company.\n        c. Waive such conditions Precedent and proceed to Closing; or\n        d. Rescind this Agreement.\n\n6.2\tFulfillment of Conditions Precedent\n\n6.2.1.\tThe Parties shall co-operate and use their best endeavours to ensure, fulfill or procure the fulfillment of the Conditions Precedent on or before the Closing Date\n. \n6.2.2.\tIf at any time any Party becomes aware of any circumstances that will or are likely to give rise to the non-fulfillment of any Condition Precedent by the Closing Date, then such Party shall immediately give to the other Parties written particulars of any such circumstances  and the Parties hereto shall co-operate fully with a view to procuring fulfillment of the relevant Condition Precedent.\n\n6.2.3\tThe “AS Group” shall ensure that all the returns,  forms, annual accounts, income tax returns, and all such  other documents that the Company ought to have filed since its incorporation with the Registrar of Companies, Jharkhand and such other statutory authorities, as may be applicable, have been duly filed either within the respective due dates or thereafter on the payment of additional fees / late fees, as the case may be.\n\n6.2.4  On fulfillment of the Conditions Precedent, the Company  and the “AS Group” shall provide written confirmation of the  same (the “CP Confirmation”) to The “Khemani Group”, as the case may be, within 3 (three) Business Days of fulfillment of all of the Conditions Precedent.\n\n6.3\tActions pending Closing\n\n6.3.1. The Company and the “AS Group” shall ensure that on and from the date of execution of this Agreement until the Closing Date, the Company will carry on its business in all material respects in the ordinary and usual course with due care and diligence and in the manner and scope carried on prior to the date of execution  of this Agreement.\n\n6.3.2\tWithout prejudice to the generality of Article 6.3.1, the Company and the “AS Group” shall not without the prior  written consent of The “Khemani Group”.\n\n7.\tCLOSING\n7.1     Closing\n7.1.1\tThe Closing shall take place within 10 (ten) days from the date of satisfaction of all of the Conditions Precedent and receipt of the CP Confirmation  by the “Khemani Group” in accordance with Article …..above.  The Closing shall take  place at the registered office of the Company or at such other place as may be agreed between the Parties in writing (the “Closing Date”)\n7.1.2. \tAll transactions contemplated by  this Agreement shall be    deemed to occur simultaneously and no such transaction shall be    consummated unless all such transactions are consummated.\n\n7.2\tAt Closing\n7.2.1.\tThe Total Share Subscription of Rs. 5,00,00,000 (Rupees Five Crores) by way of subscription money alongwith the subscription application shall be remitted to the Company by the “Khemani Group” on or before the closing date ……….;\n\n7.2.2. The “AS Group” shall deliver  to the “Khemani Group”, a  duly certified true copy of the resolution passed by the Board of the Company Allotting …………….equity shares of Rs.100 each credited as fully paid against payment made by the “Khemani Group” alongwith the relevant share certificates made in favour of the “Khemani Group” / its nominees which shall be equivalent to the number of total shares presently held by the “AS Group” ;\n\n7.2.3\tThe “AS Group” shall deliver to the “Khemani Group”, a confirmation  that all the representations and warranties contained in Article 2 hereof  are true and correct in all material respects;\n\n 7.2.4\tThe Board of Directors of the Company shall hold  an Extra Ordinary General Meeting (“EOGM”) either before or on the closing date to approve  the amendments to the Memorandum and Articles of Association of the Company which shall include inter alia an amendment to increase the Authorized Capital of the Company to Rs. 500,00,000/- (Rupees Five Crores).\n\n 7.2.5 The Board of Directors of the Company shall pass a resolution approving the appointment of two directors nominated by the “Khemani Group”.\n\n\n7.3.\tPost Closing\n7.3.1\tThe Company shall as soon as possible and in case not later than 15 days of the closing date;\n    a. file with the office of the Registrar of Companies, Jharkhand, all relevant forms, as may be required under Companies Act, 1956, with respect to (i) increase in the authorised share capital; (ii) issue and allotment of the Subscription Shares and (iii) alteration to the Memorandum and Articles of Association.  \n    b. Make necessary entries in the Register of Members evidencing the fact of the allotment of shares made in favour of the nominees of the “Khemani Group”.\n    c. Make entries in the Register of Directors, Directors shareholdings, etc., as may be necessary under the law, in respect of the appointment of Independent directors  and directors representing the “Khemani Group”. \n    d. Make necessary entries in the Register of Allotment in respect of the shares allotted to the “Khemani Group”.\n\n7.3.2\tAny other document required by the terms of this Agreement to be delivered to the “Khemani Group” by the “AS Group” at the Closing.\n\n8.\tIssue of Additional Capital – Pre - Emptive Rights\n\n8.1\tSubject to the affirmative vote of the Directors nominated and appointed by the Parties hereto, unless expressly provided in this Agreement, the Company shall not issue or allot any Convertible Instrument  and shall not issue or allot any additional Shares (“New Shares”) without first offering to the  the “Khemani Group” the New Shares in proportion  to their respective shareholding in the Company.  The Company shall give a written notice (hereinafter  referred to as “Offer Notice”) to the  the “Khemani Group” at least 30 (thirty) days prior to such proposed issue.  The Offer Notice shall state the number of New Shares proposed to be issued the proposed price and the other terms and conditions of the proposed issue.  The Offer Notice shall also state the number/quantity, offer price, terms of payment of New Shares offered to each of the Shareholders.\n\n        8.2 Upon receipt of the Offer Notice, the Shareholders shall have the right to subscribe for and purchase such number of New Shares on a pro rata basis in proportion to their respective shareholding in the Company.\n\n8.3\tThe  “Khemani Group” and the “AS Group” shall indicate in writing their acceptance to subscribe to the New Shares on the terms and conditions as proposed in the Offer Notice prior to the expiry of the 30 (thirty) day period, failing which it shall be deemed to have been declined.  If any of the “Parties”  (the “Renouncing Shareholder”) declines to purchase the New Shares, it shall offer to renounce its entitlement to the New Shares in favour of the other “Party”, who have exercised in full their entitlement to the New Shares, in proportion to their shareholding at the same price and on the same terms and conditions. \n\n8.4\tThe consideration for the issue and allotment of the New  Shares shall be cash, unless otherwise approved by the Parties or if effected by  capitalization of reserves. \n\n8.5     All amounts payable in respect of any such further issue of Shares by the  Company shall be called for from time to time as may be decided by the Company after taking into account the financial requirements of the Company or as per the terms of the issue of such Shares. \n          The issue price for any New Shares will be market  value  based depending on the pricing quotes received from other interested Parties and/or on the valuations determined  by mutually agreed upon investment bankers. \n\n 9.       Transfer of Shares\n 9.1\tRight of first Offer\n9.1.1\tEach of the parties hereto grants a  right of first offer to the other Party to this Agreement (the “Offerees”), with  respect to the transfer of any or all of its Shares or any legal or beneficial interest therein (the “Offered Shares”) held by the Offeror in the Company. Accordingly, notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained herein, if any Party desires to transfer the Offered Shares, it shall offer in writing to sell the Offered Shares (the “Offer Notice”) to  the other Party, specifying:-\n\n(a)\tthe number of Offered Shares in the aggregate;\n    (b) the price at which such transfer will be made (the “Offer Price”).\n(c )   the terms and conditions upon which the Offeror is willing to transfer the Offered Shares (“Offer Terms”); and\n(d)    in the event of the Offeror proposing to transfer the Offered Shares to any person who is primarily engaged in a business which is the same as and competing with the main business of the Company or any Subsidiary, the name of such person.  Such Offer Notice shall be given on terms that such notice shall be irrevocable, except with the unanimous consent of the Offerees. \n\n9.1.2\tThe offer for sale of the Offered Shares in the Offer Notice shall be valid  for a period  of thirty (30) days from the date of receipt of the Offer Notice by the Offerees (the “Offer Period”)\n\n 9.1.3. If all the Offered Shares are accepted by the Offerees within the Offer Period, completion of the sale shall take place at the offices of the Company where the relevant Offered Shares together with duly executed transfer forms by the Offeror shall be delivered to the Offerees against payment of the relevant Offer Price.\n 9.1.4 If the Offerees offer to purchase more than all the Offered Shares then the Offerees shall have the right to purchase the Offered Shares in proportion to the Shares held by them  …\n 9.1.5 \tIf any of the Offered Shares are not accepted by the Offerees, the Offeror may transfer to any person such Offered Shares not accepted by the Offerees within three (3) months after the expiry of the Offer Period at any price not lower than the Offer Price and on the Offer Terms.  \n 9.1.6. Unless otherwise expressly provided in this Agreement, the right of any Offeror to transfer its Shares to any other person is subject to and conditional upon:\n\n(a)\tthe transferee executing the Deed of Adherence pursuant to which the combined and collective rights of the Offeror and the transferee shall not exceed the rights of the Offeror hereunder; and \n\n    (b) the transferee obtaining the written approval, consent, permission or exemption, if required, of the relevant authority for the transfer of the Shares. \n\n 9.1.7. The certificate or certificates representing the Shares shall bear the following legend:  “Transfer, pledge, charge, lien or creation of any third party rights or interest in respect of any of the Shares represented by this certificate  and the exercise of the voting rights of  such Shares are restricted by and subject to the benefits of the Subscription and Shareholder’s Agreement dated ……………….. 2007, as amended  from time to time.\n\n9.1.8. The Parties  agree that, in order to ensure compliance with the restrictions referred to herein, the Company may issue appropriate “stop  transfer” instructions to its transfer agents, if any, and that, if the Company  handles the transfer of Shares, it may make appropriate notations to the same effect in its own records. \n\n 9.1.9        The Company shall not:\n\na)    Transfer on its books any Shares that have been sold or     otherwise transferred in violation of any of the provisions of this Agreement; or \n\nb)    treat as owner of such Shares or to accord the right to vote or pay  dividends to any purchaser or other transferee to whom such Shares shall have been so transferred.\n\n 10.\t Shareholders Meetings & Board Meetings\n10.1.\tThe quorum for all general meetings of the Company shall not be less than 2 (Two) persons and must include at least one authorized representative each of the “AS Group” and The “Khemani Group” at the beginning and throughout the meetings (unless either of the Party previously grants a written waiver to the presence of its Director).   If within half an hour of the time appointed for the meeting, a quorum is not present, the meeting shall be adjourned to the same day one week later at the same time and place.  Such adjourned meeting shall also require the minimum quorum. If the quorum is also not present at the Adjourned meeting, then a fresh notice of the Meeting shall be issued as may be decided by the Board.\n\n10. .2\tThe business of the Company shall be managed by a professional managers appointed by the “Board” who shall be under the direction and supervision of the Board. The Board shall consist of not more than 7(Seven) Directors, including two nominees of the “AS Group”, two nominees of the “Khemani Group” and three Independent Directors. The Board shall exercise all such powers of the Company and do all lawful acts and things that are not, by the Act, the Memorandum and Articles of Association or this Agreement, specifically directed or required to be exercised or undertaken by the Shareholders of the Company.  \n\n10 .3\tThe Chairman of the of the Board of Directors of the Company shall be one amongst the independent directors and shall be appointed in consultation with the “AS Group”. Normally, the senior most and experienced amongst the Independent Directors shall be appointed as the Chairman of the Company.  The Directors shall be reimbursed actual expenses incurred by them for attending the Board/Committee meetings, apart from the sitting fee, as deemed appropriate by the board from time to time and depending upon the profitability of the Company.  \n\n10.4 \tThe Directors shall not be required to hold any qualification shares, Directors nominated by the Parties shall not be liable to retire by rotation.  The Parties may nominate an Alternate Director in place of any director and no party shall object to such appointment and the Board shall appoint such person as an Alternate for such Director. \n\n10.5 \tEvery Committee appointed by the board shall have at least one nominee each of the “AS Group” as well as the “Khemani Group”, respectively. \n\n10.6 \tAt least 7 (seven) days written notice shall be given to each of the Directors of any meeting of the Board provided always that a shorter  period of notice may be given with the prior written consent of the Directors.  Such written notice to the Directors shall be given at the usual address of the Directors in India and in the case of Directors not ordinarily residing in India or currently  out of India, the same shall be given at such address as notified by the concerned Director as a valid address for the service of notices for the time being.  A copy of any document(s) to be reviewed  and discussed at such meeting shall accompany such notice unless otherwise agreed by the Directors in writing. \n\n10.7  \tEvery notice convening a meeting of the Board shall set out the agenda in full and sufficient details of the business to be transacted thereat and no item or business shall be discussed or voted upon at such meeting  unless the same has been stated in full and sufficient detail in the notice convening the meeting.\t\n\n10.8 \tThe quorum for all Board Meetings shall be 3 (Three) Directors or one-third of the total strength of the Board, whichever is higher.  No quorum shall be dully constituted for any Board Meeting, unless at the commencement of the Board Meeting and during its continuation at least one (1) Director appointed by each of the Parties is present alongwith an Independent Director unless the Parties previously grant a written waiver to the presence of their Director.   If within half an hour of the time appointed for the meeting, a quorum is not present, the meeting shall be adjourned to the same day 1 (One) week later  at the same time and place.   If at any such adjourned meeting, a quorum is not constituted within 30 minutes of the time appointed for such adjourned meeting, a fresh notice of the meeting shall be issued.    The Board shall operate by majority vote. However, the Chairman shall not have casting vote in case of tie on any business and it would be considered that the resolution has not been passed by the Board.\n\n10.9 \tThe Board may act either in a meeting or through circular resolution, or in any other legally permissible manner, on any matter, except matters that  by law may only be acted upon at a Board Meeting or exclusively by or with the consent of the Shareholders.  \n\n10.10 \tThe company shall maintain an arms-length relationship  with any Connected Persons and will execute necessary contracts to offer or to receive services from  them, prior to the investment by the Parties.  For as long as the Parties own any Shares; neither the Company nor any subsidiary of the Company shall acquire any interest in, engage or transact  any business with, or enter into, modify or terminate any agreement, contract, understanding or arrangement, whether written or oral, with Connected Persons, unless such acquisition, engagement, transaction, agreement, contract, understanding, modification of terms, termination or arrangement has been approved by the Parties in writing.  Further, any and all items of compensation to an Affiliate for services as an officer, employee or consultant of or to the Company shall require the approval of the Parties. \n\n11. RESERVE MATTERS AND ACCOUNTING & AUDITING\n\n        11.1 Reserve Matters: During the currency of this agreement between the “AS Group” and the “Khemani Group” neither the Board (in physical meeting or by passing resolution through circulation or other wise) nor General Meeting (in physical meeting or by passing resolution through circulation or other wise) of “the Company” shall consider any of the following matters (Reserve Matters) without the prior consent of the “Parties”.\n    a. sell or otherwise dispose of any part of its assets for any interest therein) or contract  to do so otherwise than in the ordinary course of its business;\n    b. alter the number of Directors on the Board or appoint any additional Directors on the Board or otherwise change its key management personnel, save and except as provided in this Agreement;\n    c. Change its auditors including internal auditors;\n    d. Amend its Memorandum and Articles of Association;\n    e. Change its financial year;\n    f. Acquire assets (or any interest therein) or contract to do so, otherwise than in the ordinary course of its business or issue or acquire any Shares or other securities (including any option, warrant or other similar instruments which entitles the holder to subscribe  or acquire equity or preference shares);\n    g. Enter into any arrangement, contract or agreement with any Affiliate  or any other Person for a transaction value in excess of Rs. 50,000/- (Rupees Fifty thousand only) and/or otherwise than in the ordinary course of business and on an arms length basis and termination of key commercial contracts;\n    h. Create any additional Encumbrance over any of the assets or securities of the Company;\n    i. Declare, pay or make any dividend or distribution on the Sale Shares or other securities of the Company.\n    j. Commence any case, proceeding or other action for voluntary liquidation/winding up of the company;\n    k. Consent to entry of any judgment or enter into any settlement with its debtors; and \n    l. incur any long term debts or increase working capital drawls  above Rs……………………(Rupees …………… lac only);\n    m. Approval of audited Financial Statement of “The Company”\n    n. Approval of any amendments to the Business Plans.\n\n        11.2 ACCOUNTING & AUDITING: \n            11.2.1 The regular fiscal year of the Company shall be the year beginning on April 1st and ending on March 31st of the following year unless otherwise mutually agreed between The “Khemani Group” and one of the “AS Group”.  The books and records of the Company shall be maintained in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (“GAAP”) of India and shall correctly reflect the Company’s financial position.  Such records and supporting documents shall be available for inspection by the “Parties”, or their respective nominees at all reasonable times at the office of the Company.\n            11.2.2  The “Parties” hereto  agree to cause the books and records of the Company to be audited at the end of each fiscal year during the term of this Agreement by an accounting firm of renowned skill and integrity. (Refer Para 4.5) The  parties shall cause the Company to and the Company shall prepare annually, financial statements which shall be audited as per Applicable Law.  Such financial statements shall be provided to The “Khemani Group” and the “AS Group” at the Company’s expense.  Subject   to the approval of the meeting of shareholders such financial statements shall be final and binding  upon the  Parties as to the revenue, costs, fees,  expenses, losses and profits of the Company, in the absence  of manifest error or   fraud.\n            11.2.3 During the term of this “Agreement” and in so far as the Parties remain shareholders of the Company, the Company shall provide to each Party periodic reports.  The requirements of the periodic reports will be mutually agreed  between the Parties.\n            11.2.4 The external / statutory auditors, a practicing Chartered Accountants firm in India, will be nominated and appointed with the consent of The “Khemani Group” and the “AS Group”.\n \n12. DISTRIBUTION OF PROFITS\nEvery  year, the Board of directors will decide the amount of profits that need to be retained in the Company for expanding the operation of the Company, both as required  by law as well as the needs of the Company, and the amount to be recommended for shareholders approval to be distributed to the Parties as dividend, in proportion to their respective shareholding in the Company.\n \n13. PAYMENT AND TAXES\n\n13.1.\tAny and all payments to be made to the “Parties” by the Company in consequence of or  in connection with the acts or  transactions contemplated by this  Agreement and including but not limited to dividends, interest payments and “reimbursable  expenses, shall be made, except as otherwise provided herein  at bank or such  other address in India,  as may be  designated from time to time in writing by the “Parties” to the Company. \n\n14. Intellectual Property Rights / Proprietary Information\n\n14.1    Any agreement to grant or avail any IPR developed and owned by the Company, on a license or other arrangement will require the affirmative vote of the Parties. \n\n 14.2.  The Parties recognize  that each of them may be given and has access to \tconfidential and proprietary information of the other Parties.  The parties  undertake not to use any such confidential information, other than for purposes related to this Agreement and/or protecting their respective interests under this Agreement and/or in the Company without the prior written consent of the other Parties and shall use their best efforts to keep confidential  and not disclose to any third party save and except on a “need-to-know” basis any confidential information of the other Parties.  The provisions of this Article shall not apply to confidential information which; \n\na)\tis or becomes part of the public domain without breach of this Agreement by a Party:\nb)\tis lawfully in the possession of a Party and subject to an existing agreement between the Parties. \nc)\tis received from a third party who lawfully acquired such information  without restriction, and without a breach of this Agreement by a Party, and / or \nd)\tis released pursuant to a binding court order or governmental regulation, provided that the Party delivers a copy of such order or action to the Company and co-operates  with the Company if it elects to contest such disclosure.\n\nThe provisions  of this Article shall survive the termination of this Agreement.\n\n15.\tTermination \n15 .1\tThis agreement shall remain in force unless terminated by mutual consent by the Parties. In the event of the parties terminating this agreement, either of the Parties can choose to purchase the shares of the other party at a price that may be determined by the Statutory Auditors namely  Delloitte Haskins & Sells. The Parties agree that the KHEMANI GROUP shall have the first right to exercise the option of buying the shares from the “AS Group” or vice versa.\n\n15 2 \tThis agreement may be terminated by any of the parties (aggrieved party) for a breach of any of the articles of this agreement committed by the other party unless the aggrieved party waives such breach by the other party. \n\n15.3 \tThis Agreement shall become effective from the Effective Date and shall remain in full force and effect until the parties mutually decide to     terminate the agreement\n\n16.\tNon-Compete \nThe “Parties” hereto agree that if either of the Parties decides to set up another brewery or acquire another existing brewery and / or distilleries within the States of Jharkhand, Bihar, Chhatisgarh and West Bengal, then in such an eventuality the party intending to set up or acquire a brewery, as the case may be, shall offer to the other party  an opportunity   to be associated with that project as a promoter in the same proportion  as the respective share holding of the Parties are in the Company at the relevant time. The offer shall be made in writing to the other Party at the earliest possible time and a period of 60 (sixty) days should be given for accepting or rejecting the said offer. If no response is received from the Offeree after the expiry of the said period of sixty days it shall be deemed that the Offeree has waived its right in this regard and the same shall be irrevocable. \n\n16.1.\tThe Parties agree that during the term of this Agreement and for a period of three (3) years after termination of this Agreement: \n\n16.1.1.  \tThe Parties  shall not in any manner provide or divulge any IPR or any information in any manner and form whatsoever for the purpose of and/or relating to the rendering, selling, supplying, marketing or distributing of products or services constituting part of the Business including rendering any assistance for the purpose of improving, modifying, upgrading or making any betterment to any existing process, know-how, software methodology or technology whatsoever for the purpose of and/or relating to the manufacturing, selling, supplying, marketing or distributing of the same whether or not the same is patented or proprietary  or otherwise; and this covenant shall be interpreted in the widest possible commercial sense and shall be observed, in letter and in spirit.\n16.1.2. In the event any of the Parties transfers its Shares, the provisions of this Article shall apply to such Party for a period of three (3) years succeeding the date on which the Board accepts the transfer of his / its Shares.\n\n17. \tArbitration and Jurisdiction                                                 \n\n17.1 \tIn the event any disputes or differences arise in connection with the interpretation, implementation or purported termination of this   Agreement as specified above, the Parties shall attempt in the first    instance to resolve such dispute through friendly consultations.\n17.2 \tIf such dispute is not resolved through friendly  consultations within thirty (30) days after commencement of discussions or such longer period as the Parties agree to in writing, then any Party may refer the dispute for resolution by arbitration in accordance with the provisions of Article 17.3 of this Agreement.\n17.3 \tAll such disputes shall be referred to and finally resolved by arbitration pursuant to the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 thereof, amendment or re-enactment thereto  from time to time and under the Rules  of the Indian Council of Arbitration (“ICA”), which Rules are deemed to be incorporated by reference into this Article.  The Tribunal shall consist of one arbitrator mutually selected and appointed by all Parties  to the dispute other than the Company, or failing such agreement three arbitrators appointed as follows:\n    • All of whom shall be fluent in English.  \n    • The Parties hereto shall appoint one arbitrator each and the two arbitrators shall appoint the third arbitrator.   \n    • It is clarified that the Company, even if a party to the dispute, shall not be entitled to select or appoint any arbitrator.  \n    • The language of the arbitration  shall be English.  \n    • The arbitration award shall be final and binding on the Parties and the Parties agree to be bound thereby and to act accordingly.\n    • The arbitrators may (but shall not be required to) award to the Party that substantially  prevails on merits, its costs and reasonable expenses (including legal costs).\n    • When any  dispute is under arbitration, except for the matters under dispute, the Parties shall continue to exercise their remaining respective rights and fulfill their remaining respective obligations under this Agreement to the extent practicable. \n\n17.4\tSubject to the provisions of Article 17.3, the Court having  jurisdiction under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 to determine under all matters that the court is entitled to determine thereunder, including without limitation provision of interim relief under the provisions of Section 9 of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 shall be the courts at Ranchi only.\n\n17.5.\tThis Agreement shall be governed, construed, interpreted and given effect of according to the laws of India.\n\n18. Force Majeure    \nNo Party shall be liable to the other Parties for delay or failure to perform under this Agreement caused by an event or occurrence of Force Majeure.  As  used herein “Force Majeure” shall mean any cause or circumstance outside the reasonable control of the Party seeking the protection of this Article including, hostilities, revolution, terrorism, civil commotion, strike, epidemic, accident, fire, lightning, flood, storm, earthquake (and any other Acts of God) explosion, blockade or embargo, or any law, proclamation, regulation or ordinance, demand, act or requirement of any government having or claiming to have jurisdiction over the subject matter of this Agreement or over the Parties.  The Party whose performance is affected by an event of Force Majeure shall promptly notify the other Parties of the existence and cessation of such event.  The Parties shall take all reasonable steps within their power to recommence performance of the Agreement following an event of Force Majeure. \n\n19. \tGeneral \n19.1.  Equitable Remedies : Each Party acknowledges and agrees that monetary damages may be an inadequate remedy for breach or threatened breach of the provisions of this Agreement, and each party agrees that, notwithstanding anything to the contrary herein, in the event of a breach of any provisions of this Agreement,  the respective rights and obligations hereunder shall be enforceable by specific performance or injunctive remedy in any court of competent jurisdiction.  The Company hereby agrees that the Shares are a unique property that cannot be readily obtained on the open market and that the Parties will be irreparably injured if this Agreement is not specifically enforced.  Therefore, the Parties shall have the right specifically to enforce the performance of the Company under this Agreement without the necessity of posting any bond or other security, and the Company hereby waives the defense in any such suit or action that the Parties have an adequate remedy at law and agrees not to interpose any opposition, legal or otherwise, as to the propriety  of specific  performance as a remedy.   The remedy of specifically enforcing any or all of the provisions of this Agreement in accordance with this Article shall not be exclusive of any other rights which the Parties may have to terminate this Agreement or of any other rights or remedies which the Parties may otherwise have, all of which rights and remedies shall be cumulative. \n\n19.2.\t Entire Agreement.  This Agreement (including the Annexures and Schedules and the other agreements or instruments executed in connection with the consummation of the Transaction) contains the entire agreement among the parties with respect to the transactions and other matters covered by this Agreement, and supersede all prior agreements, written or oral, with respect thereto.  Changes in or additions to this Agreement may be, made only upon prior written consent of the Company and Parties.  If at any time any Party shall waive its rights accruing to it, due to breach of any of the provisions of this Agreement, such waiver shall not be construed as constituting waiver of other breaches of the same kind or other provisions of this Agreement.  None of the terms of this Agreement shall be deemed to have been waived or altered, unless such waiver or alteration is in writing and is signed by all the Parties. \n\n19.3  Severability :   In the event that any one or more of the provisions contained in this Agreement shall be invalid, illegal or unenforceable in any respect under any applicable law, the validity, legality and enforceability of the remaining provisions contained herein shall not in any way be affected or impaired thereby and the Parties agree to renegotiate  such provisions in good faith.  In the event the Parties cannot renegotiate such provisions, then \n    • such provisions shall be excluded from the Agreement; and \n    • the remainder of the agreement shall be interpreted as if the provisions were so excluded; and \n    • the remainder of the Agreement shall be enforced in accordance with its terms. \n\n19.4.\t Binding Effect:   All covenants, agreements, representations, warranties and undertakings contained in this Agreement by and on behalf of any of the Parties hereto shall bind and inure to the benefit of the respective successors and assigns of the Parties hereto, whether so expressed or not.  This Agreement shall inure to the benefit of and be binding upon the Parties, their successors-in-interest and permitted assigns, but shall not be assigned by any Party without the prior written consent of the other Parties.\n\n19.5.\tNotice :   Any notices or consents or communications required to be given or served by any of the parties hereto on the other in respect of this Agreement, shall be given in writing in English  to the others, and shall be deemed to have been duly served, after 48 hours if sent by prepaid registered mail with acknowledgement due at the following address:\n\n\t(1) ………………………………………………………………….\t\n\t(2) ………………………………………………………………….\n\n19.6.\tAmendments:  No amendment, modification or variation of this Agreement shall be  binding on any Party unless and to the extent that such amendment, modification or variation is recorded in a written document executed by such Party, but where any such document exists and is so signed such  Party shall not allege that such document is not binding by virtue  of an absence of consideration.\n\n19.7.\tMemorandum and Articles:   The parties hereto agree that the terms of this agreement shall be incorporated in the Memorandum and Articles of Association to the extent possible. If any provisions of the Memorandum or the Articles of Association (as amended from time to time) are in conflict  with any of the  provisions of this Agreement, the provisions of this Agreement shall prevail and the Parties shall, whenever necessary, exercise all voting and other rights and powers available to them to procure the amendment of the Articles of Association to the extent necessary  to permit the Company and its affairs to be carried out as provided in this Agreement. \n\n19.8.\tCommunication: The Company and the Parties understand that communication sent  via facsimile machines, Internet, diskettes or any other method over public lines is not encrypted, and these transmission methods are therefore not secure means of transmission of information.  The Company and the Parties acknowledge and accept that such unsecured transmission method involves the risk of possible unauthorized alteration and/or unauthorized uses of communication.  The Company and the Parties agree to exempt the Parties from any and all responsibility of such misuse  of communication, and to hold the Parties harmless for any costs or losses that the Company or the Parties may incur due to any errors, delays or problems in transmission between any of the Parties and the Company or any Promoter/s or otherwise caused by using facsimile machines, internet, diskettes or any method over public lines as a means of transmission.\n\n19.9\tAssignability:  This Agreement and each and every covenant, term and condition hereof shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the “Parties” hereto and their respective successors and permitted assignees, but neither this “Agreement” nor any rights or obligations hereunder shall be assignable directly or indirectly by either “Party” hereto without prior written consent of the other “Party”\n                       \n\n20. COUNTERPARTS\nThis Agreement may be executed in two or more counterparts, and by each party on the same or different counterparts, but all of such counterparts shall together constitute one and the same  instrument.\n\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF the Parties hereto have executed this Agreement on the date and the year first hereinabove written.\n\n1.\tBy the withinnamed Mr. Ajay Sinha \n\nin the presence of \n\n2.\tBy the withinnamed Mr.  Ashok Khemani\n…………………………………….\nwas hereunto affixed pursuant to a resolution \t)\npassed at the meeting of its Board of Directors \t)\nheld  on _______ by Mr……………... \t\t)\nIn the presence of \t\t\t\t\t)\n \n\n3.\tThe Common Seal of the within named “Company” \n(…………………………………\t)\nWas hereunto affixed pursuant to a resolution \npassed at the meeting of its Board of Directors \t)\nheld  on _______ by Mr…………………… \t\t)\n\n***********************\n2/11/07"});
